{"name":"Shades of Ruby","hex":"#9c0009","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shades","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shade"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sunglasses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shades"},{"term":"ruby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clear, deep, red variety of corundum, valued as a precious stone.","A deep red colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep, red color; ruby-red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ruby"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunglasses","blocks":[{"text":"Sunglasses or sun glasses are a form of protective eyewear designed primarily to prevent bright sunlight and high-energy visible light from damaging or discomforting the eyes. They can sometimes also function as a visual aid, as variously termed spectacles or glasses exist, featuring lenses that are colored, polarized or darkened. In the early 20th century, they were also known as sun cheaters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Allef_Vinicius_2016-10-20_%28Unsplash%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Allef_Vinicius_2016-10-20_%28Unsplash%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunglasses"},{"title":"Ruby","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a pinkish-red to blood-red-colored gemstone, a variety of the mineral corundum, consisting of aluminium oxide (α-Al2O3). Ruby is one of the most popular traditional jewelry gems and is very durable. Other varieties of gem-quality corundum are called sapphires, and rubies are also sometimes referred to as \"red sapphires\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Corundum-215330.jpg/330px-Corundum-215330.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby"},{"title":"Ruby (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Ruby is a color that is a representation of the color of the cut and polished ruby gemstone and is a shade of red or pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruby_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cd/Eskimo_snowgoggles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cd/Eskimo_snowgoggles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Inuit snow goggles function by reducing exposure to sunlight, not by reducing its intensity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEskimo_snowgoggles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg/500px-Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg/500px-Zoom_lunette_ardente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Antoine Lavoisier conducting an experiment related to combustion generated by amplified sun light","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZoom_lunette_ardente.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Animation_polariseur.gif/250px-Animation_polariseur.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/54/Animation_polariseur.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Animation_polariseur.gif/250px-Animation_polariseur.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Effect of pair of polarized filters","link":"https://en.wikipedi